module main

-- §8 h-level: `IsSet String` resolves as ordinary instance evidence.
--
-- 'String' is a genuine set: a sequence of unicode scalars with decidable
-- structural equality (Hedberg ⇒ UIP). This test pins the `String`
-- instance specifically — under the revised spec it is one of MANY
-- standard h-level facts, not the only one: §14.1.1 makes `IsSet a` a
-- supertrait of `Eq a` (so every required `Eq` instance of §28.2.3
-- carries `IsSet` in its coherent evidence closure), and §28.2 requires
-- `derive IsSet Nat` outright. Those companions are pinned by the
-- nat-fin-refinement bundle (positive/nat-eq-isset-member-projection,
-- positive/isset-supertrait-closure); what this file guards is that the
-- base `String` fact keeps resolving on its own, with no Eq evidence
-- bound in scope.

let strIsSet = summon (IsSet String)

--! mode check
--! assertNoErrors
